 the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{9}{16} & =3 \\\\ 4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4} & =3 \\\\ 4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =3+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{21}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-\\frac{3}{4}.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{21}{4} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{21}{16} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{16}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{3}{4}| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{16}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{4} & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{21}{16}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{4} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{4}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{21}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404336 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404336 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86414" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404336 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404336 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation $-3{x}^{2}+36x-94=0$ can be written in the form $3(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q-p.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404336 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1734459-a432-53d0-859c-83686d8f7d22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404336 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}+36x-94) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-36x+94 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-36x+94 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-36x & =-94 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-12x] & =-94 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2}-{6}^{2}] & =-94 \\\\ 3[{(x-6)}^{2}-36] & =-94\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(x-6)}^{2}-3\\cdot 36 & =-94 \\\\ 3{(x-6)}^{2}-108 & =-94 \\\\ 3{(x-6)}^{2} & =-94+108 \\\\ 3{(x-6)}^{2